            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0438" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4084</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memoranda of the Chief of the Division of Latin-American
                        Affairs of the Department of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stabler</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On Saturday, April 21, Mr. Ménos, the
                    Haitian Minister, called at the Latin-American Division by appointment and
                    informed Mr. Stabler that he had received
                    a cable from his Government stating that the President of Haiti had held
                    numerous conferences with General Cole,
                    of the forces in occupation, in connection with Haiti’s entrance into the war
                    with Germany on the side of the United States; that General Cole had conveyed to the President a statement that it
                    would be advisable for Haiti to take this step, but that the President, in view
                    of possible opposition, desired to be assured of proper aid and assistance in
                    case the Government of Haiti decided to break relations with Germany and declare
                    war. Mr. Stabler said that he would
                    immediately take up this matter with the Secretary <pb facs="0439" n="267"
                        xml:id="pg267"/> who would then instruct him to answer Mr. Ménos’ inquiry in the premises. Mr. Ménos said he would be glad to have this
                    information as soon as possible.</p>


                <xi:include href="d356-a1.xml" xpointer="d356-a1"/>
            </div>
